      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A config file won't do much good when all the plausible user-facing options to configure have been removed from VRChat's downstream yt-dlp fork. Additionally, implementing this would increase the plausibility of user induced breakage and the amount of support requests to be handled - think of people changing `player_js_variant`, `player_js_version` and `player_client`. When users are given the chance to \"fix\" something without expertise to understand the underlying issue, users will follow instructions from the Internet blindly that may work temporarily but break later and cause headaches for others to solve.\n\nIt'd also be more powerful or potentially useful (yet less secure) to allow configuring a custom yt-dlp path in `%LocalAppdata%Low\\VRChat\\VRChat\\config.json`, rather than only allowing to configure VRChat's yt-dlp options. I would only support this option, if VRChat would release their yt-dlp source code changes and the custom `vrcrustyscript` JS runtime they use.\n\nIf the point is to allow configuring cookies / PO tokens for YouTube `ios` formats (muxed 1080p), now that would be a much better and secure idea than full unrestricted upstream yt-dlp in VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
