  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-03-25T22:03:11.846Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Some users may have a reason to change the options that `yt-dlp` gets invoked with, such as adding cookies to make YouTube videos load more reliably or to set custom format options to reduce the bandwidth utilized by downloading videos.\n\nRight now, users are turning to third-party tools to help alleviate some of these problems. While these tools are indeed very useful (as I can attest to), they run the risk of getting one's account banned if the program in question violates VRChat's Terms of Service. To reduce the reliance on third-party tools, I suggest adding some sort of way to configure the options that `yt-dlp` gets invoked with.\n\nI think a good way to implement this sort of thing is to have VRChat's `yt-dlp` read from a config file specific to `yt-dlp` stored in the same directory as the other configuration files for VRChat. By implementing it this way, it remains out of the way for normal users so that they don't accidentally break video downloading, yet it gives advanced users the ability to change how `yt-dlp` downloads videos to better suit their needs or fix any issues they may run into.",
